# TASK-005 red run: ./mvnw verify -Dskip.frontend=true -Djacoco.skip=true -Dmaven.test.failure.ignore=true -Dtest='CancellationReasonTest,RefundRecordMigrationTest,AppendOnlyArchTest' -Dit.test='Cancellation*IT'
# surefire (CancellationReasonTest, RefundRecordMigrationTest, AppendOnlyArchTest) and failsafe (Cancellation*IT): 38 assertion failures and 25 errors, 0 compile errors.
# Every error is a missing-implementation error, not a test defect: 22 integration tests and 2 migration tests hit 'Table REFUND_RECORD not found' (BadSqlGrammar) when they take their before-snapshot or insert a row, because V11 is added in the green commit
#   (a committed migration is never edited, so the schema is written once, with its tests already in place); the AppendOnlyArchTest 'set-wide' check errors because RefundRecordEntity and RefundRecordRepository do not exist yet. Every other failure is an assertion.
# Production stub: domain.cancellation.CancellationReason (the four names, parse() recognises none). Absent on purpose: V11, RefundRecordEntity, RefundRecordRepository (AppendOnlyArchTest existence checks fail while absent), CancellationService, CancellationController.
# The cancel and preview endpoints do not exist, so MockMvc answers 404/405 and every API test fails on its status assertion. The CancellationReasonTest cases that expect 'not a reason' pass with the stub (it recognises nothing); 'each parses to itself' fails.
# IDs covered: AC-08.1 (worked example, defaults, reasons, per-product fee, premium basis, date window, shape, P-5 order, early renewal), AC-08.2 (cooling-off and its boundaries), AC-08.3 (floor), AC-08.4 (one record, second cancel, race, atomicity, ArchUnit, migration),
#   AC-10.2 (endorse after a real cancel), AC-10.3 (LAPSED by the real cycle), AC-10.4 (sequences with a real cancel), NFR-03.1 (log capture), NFR-04.1 (roles, 404, no challenge), NFR-04.3 (415), NFR-04.4 (413 incl. percent-encoded path), NFR-05 (V1 to V10 checksums, V11 next)

